              <h2>WaitWell — Patient Communication SaaS Platform</h2>
              <p>WaitWell is a full-stack SaaS application focused on real-time patient communication and visit tracking. The project was built to reduce uncertainty by giving patients, staff, and administrators a clearer view of the care process.</p>
              <p>As the full-stack developer and project maintainer, I implemented role-based system authentication, Supabase-backed data handling, responsive UI components, and production-ready delivery workflows with CI/CD, branch protection, code reviews, and automated testing.</p>

              <div class="features mt-4">
                <h3>Key Features</h3>
                <div class="row gy-3">
                  <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="feature-item" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="400">
                      <i class="bi bi-person-check-fill"></i>
                      <h4>Role-Based Authentication</h4>
                      <p>Built authentication and authorization flows so patients, staff, and administrators could access the right parts of the platform.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="feature-item" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="500">
                      <i class="bi bi-arrow-repeat"></i>
                      <h4>Real-Time Visit Tracking</h4>
                      <p>Delivered a live patient communication flow so users could see progress and status updates during their visit.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="feature-item" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="600">
                      <i class="bi bi-database-fill"></i>
                      <h4>Supabase Data Layer</h4>
                      <p>Used Supabase to manage application data and keep the platform structured for production use.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="feature-item" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="700">
